There are a total of $\binom{15}{3} = 455$ ways to choose three articles of clothing from the drawer.

To get one shirt, one pair of shorts, and one pair of socks, we need to choose one shirt out of the 4 available, one pair of shorts out of the 5 available, and one pair of socks out of the 6 available. This can be done in $\binom{4}{1} \cdot \binom{5}{1} \cdot \binom{6}{1} = 4 \cdot 5 \cdot 6 = 120$ ways.

