\[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
x^2 + 1 &\text{ if } x > 5, \\
2x - 3 &\text{ if } -5 \leq x \leq 5, \\
3 &\text{ if } x < -5.
\end{array}
\right.\]

solution_steps:
We can subtract vectors component-wise, so
\[\mathbf{a} - 3 \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -7 \\ 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - 3 \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -7 \\ 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 12 \\ 6 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -7 - 12 \\ 0 - 6 \\ 1 - (-3) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -19 \\ -6 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}.\]
Therefore, $\mathbf{a} - 3 \mathbf{b} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -19 \\ -6 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}}.$The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}-19\-6\4\end{pmatrix}

