To determine the least common multiple (LCM) of two numbers, we can use the prime factorization method.
First, we find the prime factorization of each number.
\begin{align*}
1332 &= 2^2 \cdot 3^2 \cdot 37 \\
888 &= 2^3 \cdot 3 \cdot 37
\end{align*}
Next, we take the highest power of each prime factor that appears in either prime factorization.
\begin{align*}
2^3 &= 8 \\
3^2 &= 9 \\
37 &= 37
\end{align*}
Finally, we multiply these highest powers together to find the LCM.
\begin{align*}
8 \cdot 9 \cdot 37 &= \boxed{2664}
\end{align*}
The answer is: 2664

