We are given a square with side length 10, and two congruent equilateral triangles are drawn inside the square such that they share one side and each has one vertex on a vertex of the square.
To find the side length of the largest square that can be inscribed in the space inside the square and outside of the triangles, we need to determine the length of the side of this square.

Let's draw lines to divide the space inside the square and outside of the triangles into different regions. 

[asy]
